  "notes": "Runnymeade Avenue: the name RUNNYMEADE is printed south of Hoffner (50 ft) and the word AVENUE on the same line north of Wolcott (60 ft); read as one street from Powers to Colerain, with a small jog at Hoffner (centre x about 1839 north, 1828 south). The line near x 1805 in it is a water pipe. Hanifield Street is printed both on the north-south street meeting Colerain at x 1568 and along the top edge east of Jerome; its west edge and the bend between the two legs are off the plate, so the Colerain T centre assumes the 60 ft width from the east edge. Hanifield/Jerome: top street cut by the plate edge, centre y uncertain (+-30). Powers Street is cut by the bottom neat line (about y 7200); north edge y 7140-7145, centre taken near the neat line, uncertain +-30 in y. Hoffner Avenue is drawn only about 70 px wide (printed 25). West Fork Road (top left) meets Colerain off the top edge: not picked. Unnamed 12 ft alley between Cass and Herron (x about 720-735, Hoffner to Powers): not picked."
